From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prelude OS <prelude@local>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: zero reorder delay and tolerate parser DMA offset jitter in H.264

In low-latency phone projection (Android Auto / CarPlay), streams have
no B-frames and max_num_reorder_frames == 0. Setting bits [15:8] of
AV_SCRATCH_0 to 0 instructs the Amlogic microcode not to delay picture
emission, returning decoded frames immediately without holding them in the
DPB buffer.

Additionally, ESPARSER DMA alignment and search pattern padding can cause
the packet write pointer in VIFIFO to advance up to ~256 bytes ahead of the
actual slice header offset reported by firmware. Allow up to SZ_1K bounded
tolerance when matching VIFIFO offsets in amvdec_dst_buf_done_offset,
preventing false-positive misses and preserving accurate per-buffer
timestamp association.

Signed-off-by: Prelude OS <prelude@local>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c  | 5 ++++-
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
index 548c717..c82613b 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
@@ -316,6 +316,8 @@ static void codec_h264_set_par(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	/* End of ref MV */
 	amvdec_write_dos(core, AV_SCRATCH_4, h264->ref_paddr + h264->ref_size);
 
+	dev_info_once(core->dev, "H.264 zero-reorder low-latency: max_refs=%u, dst_bufs=%u\n",
+		      h264->max_refs, sess->num_dst_bufs);
 	amvdec_write_dos(core, AV_SCRATCH_0, (h264->max_refs << 24) |
 					     (sess->num_dst_bufs << 16) |
-					     ((h264->max_refs - 1) << 8));
+					     (0 << 8));
 }
 
 /*
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
index 6817394..c982314 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
@@ -398,7 +398,7 @@ void amvdec_dst_buf_done_offset(struct amvdec_session *sess,
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&sess->ts_spinlock, flags);
 
 	/* Look for our vififo offset to get the corresponding timestamp. */
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(tmp, n, &sess->timestamps, list) {
-		if (tmp->offset > offset)
+		if (tmp->offset > offset && (tmp->offset - offset) > SZ_1K)
 			break;
 
 		match = tmp;
-- 
2.39.5
